WEBVTT

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:05.530
Pokémon World Championships News!

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:13.380
Today, a special on the Masters Tournament,
where fierce fights are unfolding at this very moment!

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:19.490
You’ll enjoy the Masters Tournament 100,000... 1,000,000—

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.360
No, <i>10,000,000 times more</i> after watching this show!

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.510
So, let’s begin!

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:06.640
The Pokémon World Championships!

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.480
Trainers worldwide compete,
aiming to be the number one Pokémon battler!

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.430
More than 10,000 trainers entered!

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.370
And reigning over that lofty summit are...

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.620
...the Masters Eight!

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:28.840
This summer, the battles between the Masters Eight,
the Masters Tournament, have begun!

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.710
With champions hailing from various regions,
it is truly a “festival of dreams”!

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.680
The first round went from
turbulent match to turbulent match!

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.640
All eyes were on the first match,
where Competitor Dande faced Competitior Alan.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:46.690
Kyodai... max!

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:53.320
Competitor Monarch Dande immediately
chose to Daimax, to thrill the arena.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:57.700
Thanks to the power of Daimax,
Gorillander was on a roll!

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:02.580
But Competitor Alan’s ace, Lizardon,
disrupted its rhythm!

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.080
Plus!

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.880
Heed my heart’s call,
Key Stone!

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:11.960
Mega Lizardon picked up momentum
by Mega Evolving!

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:18.800
Its Dragon Claw, which has taken down
countless Pokémon, rushed for its opponent’s throat!

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:22.350
But! It was one step out of reach,

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.180
paving the way for
Competitor Dande’s victory.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:30.190
The second match pit Competitor Wataru
against Competitor Carne.

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:32.940
Have a taste of my
well-trained Dragon moves!

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:39.820
With his hyper-aggressive dragon brigade,
Competitor Wataru attacked, attacked, and attacked...

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:44.000
...but Competitor Carne used status moves
to bring her opponent to her mercy.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:49.040
The deciding factor was
Pumpjin’s Halloween!

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.400
By adding the Ghost type
to the dragon brigade,

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.130
she threw off
Competitor Wataru’s pace.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:56.830
Checkmate!

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:58.150
Moonforce!

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:04.530
After a fierce back-and-forth battle,
the referee’s fan rose for Competitor Carne.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.480
The third match pit Competitor Shirona
against Competitor Iris.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.820
Their battle began
with a surprising twist!

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.830
I’ll put my faith in Doryuzu...

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:17.890
...and bet on this attack!

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:23.620
The young Champion of Isshu landed
a low-accuracy one-hit knockout move!

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:27.240
Yet the queen of Sinnoh
was unfazed.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.510
She calmly and clearly continued to corner
her opponent, predictably dominating the match!

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:33.210
Then...!

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.950
Gaburias...

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:38.720
Mega Evolve!

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:45.180
She used Mega Evolution for the very first time
in an official match, overwhelming Ononox!

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:49.230
Competitor Shirona
won the white mark with dignity!

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:56.530
But most tumultuous of all was the fourth match,
where Competitor Daigo faced Competitor Satoshi.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:05:02.270
Competitor Daigo built upon his core steely defenses
with a variety of hard and soft attacks.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:07.080
He’s the strongest and most impressive...
Truly, the Champion of Hoenn!

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:13.180
Competitor Satoshi tried to keep up,
but couldn’t quite steal the lead.

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:18.170
At the close, Competitor Daigo
sent out his ace, Mega Metagross.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:24.390
Faced with its speed and predictive movement,
Pikachu’s paws and tail were tied!

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.210
This is Mega Metagross!

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.520
It’s predicting every movement
Pikachu makes.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:35.890
Pikachu!

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.820
Driven into a corner,
Satoshi turned to...

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:47.410
Far greater than 100,000 Volts...
1,000,000 Volts!

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:53.170
No, way, <i>way</i> greater than that!
Our super full power!

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:59.550
Pikachu! 10,000,000 Volts!

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:05.180
If one attack fails, how about two?!
If two fail, how about three?!

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.680
With seven attacks
of seven-colored electricity,

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.840
he finally caught Mega Metagross!

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:15.120
Competitor Satoshi wasted no time
in seizing this moment of opportunity!

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:19.980
Using Pikachu’s speed for a swift attack,
he conquered Mega Metagross!

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.990
Competitor Satoshi
took home the win!

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:28.550
Next up, an in-depth analysis
on the four competitors advancing to the semifinals...

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:36.500
...and the Pokémon you should keep your eyes on,
using our show’s exclusive database!

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:42.770
We’ll start with this man:
the Supreme Monarch, Competitor Dande!

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:47.090
On top of the overwhelming skills
of his well-trained Pokémon,

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:49.870
he employs genius-level
battle technique!

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:53.890
With his unmatched skills of observation,
he doesn’t miss a trick from his foes!

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:58.040
His ace is the Flame Pokémon,
Lizardon.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:01.020
Its greatest weapon
is its Kyodaimax.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:07.290
Clad in blazing wings,
its battles are heated beyond compare!

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:12.940
Next, the strong and dignified
star actress, Competitor Carne!

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:19.730
Her precisely calculated, beautifully
composited battles play out like a movie.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:24.030
Competitor Carne is an actress of
a hundred faces, and a hundred strategies!

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:27.550
Her ace is the Embrace Pokémon,
Sirknight.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:32.590
Their eye contact during battle
is a skill born from their close bond.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:37.210
What sort of scenes
will she show us in the semifinals?

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.680
Next, the Queen of Sinnoh,
Competitor Shirona!

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:45.020
“Dande the Warrior”...

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:48.950
“Shirona the Wise”... A nickname coined
due to her incredible wealth of knowledge.

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:52.200
Her experience, allowing her
to wrest victory from any situation,

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.800
is the highest of the Masters Eight!

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.910
Her ace is the Mach Pokémon,
Gaburias.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.960
Its attack, defense, and speed
are all top-class!

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:04.900
Now with the ability
to Mega Evolve, the sky—

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:08.090
No, the <i>heavens</i>
are the limit for its strength!

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:12.830
Last, the golden rookie,
Competitor Satoshi.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.530
His unpredictability is number one!

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:19.830
He took down the Dragon Storm,
Competitor Kibana, to enter this tournament!

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:25.100
Being momentum incarnate,
he advanced to the semifinals!

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.570
His battle style
can only be called crazy!

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.090
He’s anything but a safe bet,

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:32.830
but his explosive power glitters
like lightning!

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:34.930
Connecting heart-to-heart
with Pokémon,

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:38.080
he can draw out powers
nobody can foresee!

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:43.920
Our program has followed Competitor Satoshi
ever since he was in the Super Class.

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:50.450
Along with telling you which Pokémon to keep your eyes on,
we’ll be ranking his most shocking battles!

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.360
In third is... Pikachu!

00:08:55.530 --> 00:09:00.150
A brand new form of defense
that sent a stadium into an uproar!

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:07.110
Faced with Luchabull’s swift movements,
and the top-class Flying-type move, God Bird,

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:10.080
Competitor Satoshi
was set for a struggle.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:13.160
But then,
he came up with a secret plan!

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:14.490
100,000 Volts!

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:27.340
Iron Tail!

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:31.550
Dig into the ground!

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.890
Lightning Speed!

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:49.110
The power of the Lightning Speed
is making Pikachu’s body shake violently!

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.320
What could this be?!

00:09:55.620 --> 00:10:00.820
Creating hypervibrations with Lightning Speed,
he reduced the damage from God Bird!

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:05.250
Using an offensive move for defense...
It was a shocking idea!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:08.450
In second is... Kairyu!

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:12.960
Apparently, he even invented
a new move in a crazy way.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.300
So what exactly did he do?

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:21.520
It happened in a battle against Competitor Iris of the Masters Eight.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.180
Dragon Pulse!

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:29.800
Swallow it up with Hurricane!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.500
I’ve got your Dragon Pulse!

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:52.050
They took on the energy from the Dragon Pulse,
and used it for a new move!

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:54.010
But that means... No way!

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:58.350
Go! Draco Meteor!

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:13.770
Swallowing his opponent’s move with Hurricane
and reforming it into a new move!

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:17.780
Apparently, he’s polished
this Draco Meteor even further,

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:20.450
raising our hopes even higher.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:23.950
And finally,
in first place... Lucario!

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.240
An earthquake ran through the stadium!

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.460
What could this oversized
Aura power mean?!

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:36.990
Kyodaimax Duraludon was completely unfazed
by Lucario’s attacks.

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:42.470
Having lost all avenues of attack, what did
Competitor Satoshi and Lucario do next?

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:44.220
This is where it ends!

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:45.850
Roar, my dragon!

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.310
Time for my ultimate attack...
Kyodai Decay!

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:18.340
What is that...?

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:23.000
Lucario! Kyodai Aura Sphere!

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:26.350
Duraludon! Dai Rock!

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.300
Let’s go!

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:53.200
By focusing their minds, the hearts of
trainer and Pokémon united as one!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:57.150
Their heightened Aura
unleashed power beyond scale!

00:12:57.150 --> 00:13:01.050
Plus, Lucario also has
Mega Evolution in his arsenal!

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:03.390
You Mega can’t miss it!

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:08.530
Competitor Satoshi surprises us
with each and every battle.

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:13.450
How will he shock us
in the semifinals?

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:17.810
Our program supports Competitor Satoshi!

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:32.670
Everyone, thanks for waiting!

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:35.790
It’s time for
“A Dragon Dive Into Your Heart Radio”!

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:39.010
Wherever I go,
stories are sure to be found.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:42.550
Hi! Narray Sean here!

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:45.970
Life is full of up and downs,
and so are Pokémon!

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:49.020
Whether you’re Detecting, getting Detected,
or even Brutally Swung,

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:54.120
all of you who work hard at Reversals
when life doesn’t go according to plan,

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:56.010
Huh, I didn’t know there was a show like this.

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:57.020
let me take another Dragon Dive
into your hearts today!

00:13:57.660 --> 00:14:00.300
Thank you for all your
messages again this week!

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:05.810
Today’s first Dive will be into a message
from Dragon name “Silent Boy.”

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:13.140
“A friend of mine is competing
in a huge tournament.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:18.120
“I want to cheer him on, even if just a little,
so I’m sending in a message for the first time.”

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:20.740
My, you really care for that friend!

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:27.430
“He always has this dazzling smile on his face,
but I hear that he was very depressed and lonely at one point.

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:30.390
“Then, one day...”

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:35.580
Ouch!

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:40.700
Ow...

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:44.800
I’m sorry!

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:46.390
Watch yourself!

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:49.640
What’s this? You still cursed?

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:54.440
That was three years ago.
That plague has left me!

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:56.340
My luck’s perfect now!

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:01.990
You wait here, okay?

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:04.630
Don’t go anywhere, you hear?!

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:30.870
I swear... I never should have
caught that miserable Gänger.

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:34.890
Gänger?!

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:36.040
This is where you were?!

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:38.250
Wh-Why are you...?!

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:43.640
Pikachu! Electroweb!

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:50.010
Stay away! Stay away!
<i>Stay away!</i>

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:54.390
I told you to wait there,
didn’t I?

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:57.130
Nothing but trouble comes my way
when <i>you’re</i> around!

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:58.730
I’ve had enough of you!

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:00.270
That’s just cruel!

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:02.590
Shut up, shut up... shut up!

00:16:02.590 --> 00:16:04.650
Hey, wait!

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:05.710
Hey!

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:09.780
Gänger...

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:17.620
Being abandoned by its trainer
must’ve been shocking.

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:25.720
“After that, he was caught up with a bad crowd,
and completely closed off his heart.”

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:29.160
Hit by an Evil Eye
when he’s down, huh...?

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:34.510
“What finally saved that friend
were the honest and kind words of a particular boy.”

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:38.180
Forget what your old trainer said.

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:41.230
I need you... right now!

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:46.560
You don’t have to
trust me right away.

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:48.740
But just know I trust you!

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:58.970
“He’s worked hard, trying to
get stronger for that boy ever since,

00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:03.250
“and finally, he’s now competing in
a tournament to decide the world’s best.”

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.580
Now that’s love! That is love!

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:09.530
“You’re a strong, big,
and beloved friend of mine.

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:12.850
“I’m wishing with all my heart
that you’ll fight with your full power.

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:16.100
“Everything will be fine.
So hang in there, Gänger.”

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:21.300
D’aww!
You’re no “Silent Boy” at all!

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:24.690
I’m sure your friend
heard you loud and clear.

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:28.240
Oh, I’ve already had
a comment come in.

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:32.820
That’s like Lightning Speed!
Dragon name, “Man of Steel”...

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:35.860
“Dear Sir Silent Boy.

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:39.290
“Thy care for thy friend
left a deep impression upon me.”

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:41.550
So formal and stiff!
This is too much!

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:48.050
“Though I bid it chance, a student of mine
also competes in a tournament.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.670
“O, the memories.

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:54.370
“The days we strove together,
as I taught to him chivalry.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:58.880
“That despite his initial vain views,
upon bonding closer with his lord,

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:01.350
“he grew into a reliable knight.”

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:03.940
Psycho Cutter.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:13.610
I wonder what Mr. Gampi would say
if he could see you now.

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:17.420
Are you okay, Kamonegi?

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:29.860
You got my hopes up about your potential...
But I must say, I’m a bit disappointed.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:34.260
You’re still far too inadequate a foe
for my Earlade.

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:38.350
Yeah! We’re gonna keep going!

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:41.020
Oh, is that a change of attitude I see?

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:44.760
I know how hard
Kamonegi has trained!

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:47.630
I know more than anyone
that he can do better!

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:50.840
Let’s get stronger and stronger,
together!

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:58.370
Me and Kamonegi, we’re both inadequate,
but that’s why we’re gonna get stronger!

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:01.110
I believe in Kamonegi!

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:06.120
You good to go, Kamonegi?

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:15.690
Then you leave me no choice...

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.800
Earlade. Crossroad Kill!

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:20.670
Detect!

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:24.520
Consecutive Cut!

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:35.360
Infight!

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:46.080
All right!

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.530
That connected!

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:55.610
What?

00:19:57.030 --> 00:19:58.350
Th-That’s...

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:16.820
He evolved!

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.990
“Dear lord, and thy friend...

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:24.370
“By finding someone to protect,
my student has grown stronger.

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:27.750
“Now, may I join thee in bidding cheer.

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:30.010
“Glory be to Negigaknight’s future!

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:31.670
“Best regards.”

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:36.470
Perhaps only a handful
may compete in tournaments,

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:42.800
but every Pokémon has its own dramas,
and they’re as numerous as Draco Meteors.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:48.330
The show’s not over yet, but right now,
I have a super effective song for you!

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:15.330
“I’m Uonoragon!

00:22:17.300 --> 00:22:20.010
“I’m Uonoragon, and I napped too long.

00:22:20.010 --> 00:22:22.760
“When I awoke, I was all alone.

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:28.060
“A strange world. Strange creatures.

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:31.480
“But I’ll be fine!

00:22:31.480 --> 00:22:34.180
“I have my Strong Jaw!

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:39.190
“I can eat lots of food with it,

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:41.770
“and it makes me friends quick too.

00:22:42.900 --> 00:22:45.010
“Nom-nom over there...

00:22:45.010 --> 00:22:47.680
“Nom-nom over here...

00:22:48.550 --> 00:22:52.780
“My proud Strong Jaw makes everyone happy.

00:22:54.050 --> 00:22:56.690
“I’m Uonoragon, and I napped too long.

00:22:56.690 --> 00:23:01.700
“Today, yet again, I’m with my friends,
going nom-nom-nom-nom.

00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:05.490
“And they lived happily ever after.”

00:23:05.870 --> 00:23:10.870
<i>Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament News!</i>

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:13.500
The exciting semifinals
are finally about to begin!

00:23:13.960 --> 00:23:17.830
Competitor Monarch Dande
and Competitor Carne have arrived!

00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:21.350
No matter what happens,
the highlight is Pumpjin! Pumpjin! There it is!

00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:22.550
We’re live, you know?!

00:23:22.550 --> 00:23:25.810
That reminds me,
the brat boys aren’t here yet...

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:28.220
They probably just got lost somewhere!

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:29.760
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:31.420
The Semifinals I - “Sweep”

00:23:31.420 --> 00:23:33.470
Let’s all tune in, meow!

00:23:36.320 --> 00:23:37.900
Once this tournament’s over...

00:23:38.260 --> 00:23:39.980
I’m retiring from battles.

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:39.980
Huh?!

00:23:40.370 --> 00:23:43.190
We’re gonna win this,
Ms. Shirona!

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:47.140
Our battle is going to
spark a fire in me!

00:23:47.140 --> 00:23:48.620
Hypnosis!

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:53.040
Ms. Shirona...

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:55.080
She’s strong...

00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:59.030
Don’t let Ms. Shirona
set the pace!

00:23:59.030 --> 00:24:00.380
100,000 Volts!

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:07.930
Pikachu!

00:24:14.390 --> 00:24:17.730
After I beat Ms. Shirona,
I’m gonna get even stronger!

00:24:18.520 --> 00:24:21.520
I’ve longed for
a Pokémon battle like this!

00:24:21.880 --> 00:24:23.270
Charge!

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:26.990
Let’s heat things up even more!

00:24:26.990 --> 00:24:28.740
This is the only thing I’ve got!

00:24:28.740 --> 00:24:30.410
Let’s use our full power!
